BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 409 663 Tm (1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 663 Tm (The biggest gap: extreme spread. Extreme spread is the distance between the two shots farthest apart, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 751 Tm (it changes a lot from one group to the next even when nothing about the rifle has changed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 853 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 853 Tm (At the range. One five-shot group with an extreme spread of one inch could come from a rifle that usually) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 941 Tm (shoots three quarters or one that usually shoots an inch and a half. A single small group is good news,) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 1029 Tm (not proof.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 409 1131 Tm (2.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1131 Tm (Why five shots tell you little. A small group is mostly luck: the same rifle shoots groups of very different sizes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1219 Tm (and the fewer the shots, the wider the spread.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1321 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 1321 Tm (At the range. Before you believe a change made a difference, shoot enough to be sure. One good group) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 1409 Tm (after a change proves very little.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 409 1511 Tm (3.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1511 Tm (The range the truth is probably in. A confidence interval is the range your rifle's true figure probably lies in,) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1599 Tm (given the shots you have, and it shrinks as you shoot more.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1701 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 1701 Tm (At the range. If two loads' ranges overlap a lot, you do not yet know which is better. Shoot more before) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 1789 Tm (you decide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 409 1891 Tm (4.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1891 Tm (Comparing two loads. When two loads are compared on a few shots, one of them nearly always looks better,) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 1979 Tm (even when they are exactly the same.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 2081 Tm (-) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 2081 Tm (At the range. Do not pick a load from one group of each. Shoot both until GroupLab's comparison says it) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 607 2169 Tm (can tell them apart, or until you accept that the difference, if any, is too small to matter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 409 2271 Tm (5.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 2271 Tm (What is good enough? Good is set by your job, not by bragging: work out the target size and distance, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 508 2359 Tm (ask what precision gives you the hits you need.) Tj ET
BT /F1 71 Tf 1 0 0 -1 381 2461 Tm (The whole guide, with pictures and the numbers behind every sentence: grouplab.org/guides/statistics-primer/) Tj ET
